From c7e524345e305cb88cc4ee61f240d2f0ea02b033 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steedli <steed.li@nordicsemi.no>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 17:22:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [nrf noup] bluetooth: host: Add support for bonding with same
 peer

Backport of nrfconnect/sdk-zephyr#2963 to the v3.0.0 baseline so that
CONFIG_BT_ID_AUTO_SWAP_MATCHING_BONDS (added upstream after this
snapshot) is available here too.

Adds a BT_KEYS_ID_CONFLICT flag to bt_keys: set when a new bond
conflicts (same address/IRK) with a bond on another local identity.
Conflicting keys are not added to the Resolving List immediately; the
existing entry stays until the new identity actually starts
advertising/scanning, at which point bt_id_resolving_list_check_and_update()
swaps the old entry out for the new one (or returns -EPERM if the old
identity's advertiser is still running).

Adapted for this baseline's structure: keys.c's id_add() here calls
bt_id_add() directly (no BT_KEYS_ID_PENDING_ADD deferral present at
this snapshot), so the conflict-flag skip was added at that call site
instead. smp_br_id_add_replace() (BR/EDR) does not exist yet at this
baseline and was not touched.

Verified: builds and boots on nRF54L15 DK with
CONFIG_BT_ID_AUTO_SWAP_MATCHING_BONDS=y via
D:\ncs\example\mutilple_bt_id_swiftpair (branch
mutilple_bt_id_swiftpair-v3.0.0).

Signed-off-by: Pavel Vasilyev <pavel.vasilyev@nordicsemi.no>
(backported by Claude Sonnet 5 from commit 2f4f27995d80 in
nrfconnect/sdk-zephyr, found locally in D:\ncs\v3.3.1\zephyr)
